# Prefer Tailwind over custom CSS

Style UI with Tailwind utility classes in components. `globals.css` may only contain `@import "tailwindcss"` and `@theme` design tokens — no custom component classes.

## Do

- Use Tailwind utilities and theme tokens (e.g. `text-caisbe-green`, `border-ifma-border`, `shadow-brand-card`, `font-display`)
- Prefer `className` composition over inline `style` unless a value must be dynamic (e.g. measured positions)
- Extend colors/fonts/shadows only via `@theme` in `globals.css`

## Don't

- Add component-specific CSS classes, keyframes, or `body` rules in `globals.css`
- Create `.css` / `.module.css` files for new UI
- Write custom stylesheets for layout or spacing

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div className="course-card">...</div>

// ✅ GOOD
<div className="border border-ifma-border bg-white p-6 shadow-brand-card">...</div>
```
